(175, 153, 82, NULL, NULL, 'Dear EMT/Amit,\r\n\r\nPlease report following problems:\r\n\r\n1.) Pt deposition is an issue, the current is not increasing beyond 140-150mA and the DTM is also not showing the deposition rate. This is a serious issue since long time and needed to be addressed right away. Yesterday, I did my Ti/Pt deposition twice and only Ti was deposited, during Pt deposition there was overload error and gun was turned off. Previously, I faced same issue but at least Pt was getting deposited now it is not. This is recurring issue since a long time.\r\n\r\n2.) The number of pins are only 2 which can hold only 4 samples, we generally have 6 samples to be processed at the same time and we cannot use thermal tape as we also need to do back metalization. I\'ve been asking for extra pins since December when we were on clock for conference. Also Thermal Tapes are not allowed in the system according to Narayana Rao\'s mail some time back. \r\nI\'ve however put 2 pins from Al Thermal Evaporator because we are using multiple metals in 4TEBE, we cannot put those pins back in Al-Thermal Evaporator due to cross contamination issue. I used Al-Thermal Evaporator pins because we already use Al deposition in 4TEBE. If required please make new pins for Al Thermal Evaporator, but please do not put these pins back in Al-Thermal Evaporator. And while you\'re at it make some extra pins that can also be used in 4TEBE also as and when required.\r\n\r\n3.) The sweep controller issue: I have observed that the wires inside the chamber and beneath the chamber near the Air Admittance Valve are not soldered properly - they are detached. Also the PS2 connector that connects the sweep controller output to the EB Gun is loose. May be you can look in to this direction, even after performing these checks if the Sweep Controller is still not working then we need to contact HHV Engineer. I\'ve already discussed this with Pradeeep.\r\n\r\n4.) The dessicators that stores targets need to be put in Vacuum always, because the metals like Ti, Cr, Ni, Al, Yb, Gd, etc... will oxidize faster and hence make it a rule that every day put the targets in dessicator in vacuum. I\'ve already talked regarding this to Bhimraj, Kuldeep and PremSai and I think we\'ll follow this procedure from today itself. \r\n\r\nThanks & Regards', '2015-09-03 09:48:40', 2, '2015-09-11 10:00:00', '', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL),
