(818, 217, 92, NULL, NULL, 'on behalf of Prakash Sarkar.(Copied from his mail)\\r\\n\\r\\nDear sir,\\r\\nI received the mask followed by the given new pattern. The new given pattern I have attached to this mail. The optical images also of each grid I have attached by zip file. In that mask pattern there have 16 slots by naming A to P. From A to H the small dot size is 5um and I to L is 6um and M to P is 7um. From optical images I observed that none of small dots are accurately circular. For 5um small dots may be acceptable but 6um and 7um dots are not proper. Please let me know the solution because base of this mask my\\r\\nfurther research work got stuck and I want to get the proper mask as soon as possible. Kindly look into this matter.\\r\\nThanks and regards,\\r\\nPrakash', '2018-02-15 16:25:42', 2, '2018-02-16 03:05:00', 'uploads/818.zip', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(819, 217, 92, NULL, NULL, 'on behalf of Prakash Sarkar.(Copied from his mail)\\r\\nDear sir,\\r\\nI received the mask followed by the given new pattern. The new given pattern I have attached to this mail. The optical images also of each grid I have attached by zip file. In that mask pattern there have 16 slots by naming A to P. From A to H the small dot size is 5um and I to L is 6um and M to P is 7um. From optical images I observed that none of small dots are accurately circular. For 5um small dots may be acceptable but 6um and 7um dots are not proper. Please let me know the solution because base of this mask my further research work got stuck and I want to get the proper mask as soon as possible. Kindly look into this matter.\\r\\nThanks and regards,Prakash', '2018-02-15 16:28:02', 2, '2018-04-18 11:45:00', 'uploads/819.zip', 4, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(820, 725, 8, NULL, NULL, 'user tried for a-Si deposition using ICPCVD. The recipe used is attached hereby. According to XPS data, the elements in the deposited film show Si, O, N which indicates deposition of SiONx. Surprisingly with the increase in the number of runs (process time), the concentration of nitrogen increases. The XPS images are attached for your reference.', '2018-02-16 21:00:18', 2, '2018-04-18 11:42:00', '', 4, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(821, 271, 8, NULL, NULL, 'In a-Si deposition, O2 & N2 content found after XPS i.e SiOxN \\r\\nLeak test needs to be done for all MFC/Lines from Cylinder to Chamber.\\r\\n\\r\\nLeak test done from  MFC valve to chmaber for 20minPump-20minLeakTest: N2O-0.2mTorr/min, \\r\\nAr-0.03mT/min, SiH4-0.2mT/min, H2-0.02mT/min.\\r\\nLeak-up-rate of chamber: 0.05mT/min', '2018-02-19 10:37:28', 2, '2018-03-09 12:37:00', '', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL),
