(1351, 1779, 300, 'NULL', 'NULL', 'I was doing Ni deposition and while doing a ramp-up of the emission current around 20 mA, I observed all of a sudden beam had deflected enormously, and then the emission current automatically dropped down to zero and in the genius controller there was one warning popped up. Kindly find the attached image. (6. jpg)\\r\\n\\r\\n2. I observed there is one warning message no-24 which stated \\Limits are not for this source\\. When I further checked the genius controller (on a video call with prem Sai) we found every parameter (filament current, Sweep, High Voltage, Limit) changed and some default recipe was automatically loaded(\\DDDDD?\\). \\r\\n\\r\\nAs of now, I don\\\'t know whether this issue had actually done some physical damage to the tool or not. Anyway, We\\\'ll check it, But the concern is why this improper beam deflection happening at all. \\r\\n', '2023-01-06 11:53:09', 2, '2023-07-05 11:11:00', '', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL),
