(1364, 1969, 7, 'NULL', 'NULL', 'Dear Pradeep Sir,\\r\\n\\r\\nAs reported to you last Friday (20Jan 2023), while I was doing a N2 annealing run of Silicon substrates on Nano RTP system for one of the INUP users, it was observed that the preheating temperature of Pyro 1 sensor wasn\\\'t able to be reached even after 15mins of waiting. \\r\\n\\r\\nGenerally the preheating temperature which is half the annealing temperature reaches  within couple of minutes from the start of the process.\\r\\n\\r\\nMy parameters for the N2 annealing recepie were as under:\\r\\nAnnealing temperature and time - 900C for 60sec\\r\\nAnnealing gas- N2 annealing @950sccm\\r\\nPreheating temperature- 450C\\r\\nPower - 120%\\r\\nAll the Pyro and PID Calibration tables were matched as per the latest details available on the paper pasted on the tool.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nInitially it seemed that keeping a lower power percentage of 120% might have caused this but I tried with even 130% power percentage too in the 2nd run, but the result was the same and preheating temperature of 450C wasn\\\'t able to be reached again, even after 15mins of waiting.\\r\\n\\r\\nI even tried running the recepie with a different carrier wafer but to no use.\\r\\n\\r\\nImages of the process graph during one of the runs are attached for your reference.\\r\\n\\r\\nEven today I tried same recepie at 130percent power, but still the temperature isn\\\'t able to reach the preheating temperature.\\r\\n\\r\\nKindly look into this matter.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRegards,\\r\\nNikhil Palkar\\r\\nSr. Project Technical Assistant,\\r\\nCEN IITBNF, Electrical Engineering Dept,\\r\\nIITB, Powai-Mumbai.\\r\\n\\r\\n', '2023-01-27 12:55:03', 2, '2023-02-15 08:22:00', 'uploads/1364.jpg', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(1365, 1969, 7, 'NULL', 'NULL', 'This to inform that, while I tried to run an N2 annealing recepie for dopant activation run in Nano lab RTP syetem dtd 8th Feb 2023, I was facing Power overshoot issue, wherein the system power percentage contantly stayed at 1000% during the 1st annealing/soaking step of 30sec. Image attached for reference.\\r\\n\\r\\nMoreover, even though the power percentage overshooted to it\\\'s maximum level, but the Pyro1 temp still wasn\\\'t able to reach the desired annealing temperature (i.e. it stayed @850C instead of desired 950C)\\r\\n\\r\\nThe issue was so persistent that it even occurred during a dummy run which I carried out on Si substrate wafer. I had to forcefully abort the run in between, during both the runs.\\r\\n\\r\\nMy parameters for the N2 annealing recepie were as under:\\r\\nAnnealing temperature and time - 900C for 60sec\\r\\nAnnealing gas- N2 annealing @950sccm\\r\\nPreheating temperature- 350C\\r\\nPower - 130%\\r\\n\\r\\nKindly look into this matter.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRegards,\\r\\nNikhil Palkar\\r\\nSr. Project Technical Assistant,\\r\\nCEN IITBNF, Electrical Engineering Dept,\\r\\nIITB, Powai-Mumbai.', '2023-02-09 23:25:40', 2, '2023-02-17 03:03:00', 'uploads/1365.jpg', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL),
