(2042, 1987, 124, '', '', 'Tool Name: Proxima Vacuum Generating Pump  \\nModel Number: VID‑75 S  \\nManufacturer / Service Provider: Indovac Pumps &amp; Engineering Services, Bhandup (W), Mumbai\\nRequest: Gentle request for approaching with the troubleshooting to minimize noise and vibrations while turning ON Proxima&#039;s pump.\\n\\nIssue Reported:\\n- Users reported excessive noise while turning ON Proxima&#039;s pump.\\n\\nObservation:\\n- Users report high noise while Proxima system is ON.\\n- Users report higher noise while Phoenix + Proxima are ON simultaneously.\\n\\nImpact on Operations:\\n- High risk of AC power fluctuation in measurements due to high noise levels when both systems run simultaneously.  \\n- Risk of workflow disruption if spare pump fails before permanent fix.  \\n\\nActions Taken for Phoenix system&#039;s pump by EMT Team:\\n- Pump disconnected and checked in BMS room (EMT service area).  \\n- Spare dry pump connected temporarily to maintain system operation.  \\n- 5uF capacitor found faulty; samples handed over; request sent to inventory team (Mr. Jomon Simon). \\n\\nPending Request:\\n- Follow‑up with the concerned team for faulty spare-part replacement status. \\n- Since pumps for Proxima is same as that of Phoenix system, gentle request for approaching with the same troubleshooting for Proxima&#039;s pump as well to expedite resolution. ', '2025-11-21 17:50:21', 2, '2025-12-02 17:17:00', 'uploads/2042.mp4', 1, 279, 279, NULL),
