(2678, 1064, 394, '', '', 'Software testing is the process of verifying that a software application works as expected and meets its requirements. It helps identify bugs, improve product quality, and ensure reliable performance across different scenarios. This guide covers important software testing interview questions and answers for both beginners and experienced professionals, focusing on key areas like manual testing, automation, performance testing, and common tools to help with effective interview preparation.\\n\\nSoftware Testing Interview Questions For Freshers\\nBelow are the questions which cover software testing concepts for freshers preparing for interviews.\\n\\n1. What do you understand by the term SDLC in software engineering?\\nThe Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) is a structured process that outlines the different stages involved in developing software. It ensures that testing is performed at every phase to improve quality and reduce errors. The key phases include planning, requirement analysis, design, development, testing, deployment, and maintenance.', '2025-12-17 13:05:13', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 'uploads/2678.pdf', 3, 699, NULL, NULL),
