(3044, 189, 356, 'Received a complaint from Student Ekta regarding EBL Voyager', '', 'I would like to seek your guidance regarding the proximity effect correction (PEC) feature in the EBL raith/ Voyager system. I am currently facing issues during writing, particularly for highly dense patterning areas in my mask design.\\n\\nAfter EBL exposure, I observe that in certain regions the patterns have merged/submerged to a large extent, which I suspect may be due to proximity effects arising from backscattered electrons and dose accumulation in dense layouts.\\n\\nI have attached the SEM images highlighting this issue for your reference. Kindly let me know how proximity correction can be implemented or optimized in Voyager to address this problem, and whether any specific dose modulation or layout strategies are recommended for such dense patterns.', '2026-01-09 09:29:37', 2, '2026-01-27 18:00:00', NULL, 4, 189, 189, 0),
