(3261, 2501, 354, '', '', 'Initially (before December 2025), whenever I used to operate the Microwriter ML3 tool, if a user\\\'s slot was not activated, the machine never used to work (even a simple mouse movement/click/scroll never used to work). But I\\\'ve noticed it from mid-December; even if a user\\\'s slot is not activated (or not booked, or his/her slot is over), the tool is accessible. During my hands-on session on Friday (i.e., 16/01/2026), I was able to operate the machine even after my slot was over, and the user who was supposed to use that tool did not even activate his/her slot. Kindly look into it at your earliest. Although I\\\'ve informed Pankaj Gound about it in my previous 2 sessions, still no action has been taken.', '2026-01-17 16:00:40', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', NULL, 1, 89, NULL, 0),
(3262, 1829, 146, '', '', 'Gowning cabinet not available. We are calling the facility almost every time we are entering the clean room to get the gowns.', '2026-01-17 18:45:27', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', NULL, 2, 699, 297, 0),
(3263, 2149, 197, '', '', 'When Ni gun is reaching 60 W DC power, it starts flashing ARC on the controller and then gives \\\"Plasma Error\\\" and turns off. It works fine at 55 W but not at 60 W.', '2026-01-18 00:47:22', 2, '2026-02-01 19:15:00', NULL, 1, 279, 89, 0),
(3264, 2149, 137, 'Optimised spinner for Microwriter shifted to 1.2 lab', '', 'This spinner was always used for spin coating resists for lithography in Microwriter. Now the Microwriter has been shifted to NYR and this spineer has been shifted to 1.2 lab to assist with MJB4 and MJB6. The DSA spinner in NYR is not optimised for Microwriter and hence everyone is having issues with their lithography now.\\n\\nPrimary difference between both spinner is the CDA blowing syringe in PPR-AZ spinner which is absent in DSA spinner. Hence, LOR and PPR coated with DSA spinner are much thicker for the same speeds and cause issues during development.\\n\\nConsidering the exorbitant amount of usage of Microwriter compared to the combined usage of DSA, MJB4, and MJB6, it will be everyone\\\'s best interests if the PPR-AZ spinner is shifted to NYR. Please look into this.', '2026-01-18 01:12:28', 2, '2026-01-22 16:00:00', NULL, 4, 928, 928, 0),
(3265, 2149, 354, 'Baseline information on website', '', 'In the baseline information on the slotbooking module, only exposure dose and minimum feature achieved are recorded. While a standard development time is given in the baseline recipe, it says that the time may vary. \\n\\nRequest you to record development times as well for all baseline runs.\\n\\nAlso, in several cases, the sample looks developed, but post metallisation, it turns out that the samples are not properly developed.\\nPlease combine lithography baselines with metallisation baselines, so that we can get the true idea. Please include sample WITH and WITHOUT descumming.', '2026-01-18 01:56:21', 2, '2026-02-03 12:00:00', NULL, 4, 928, 928, 0),
(3266, 297, 156, NULL, NULL, 'New Building  UPS 1  Daily Reading - % Va,	Ts,	Tr,	Ti with log enter in the log sheet \\nFlag the issue if temp is above 40 C.\\nIt needs to be flag to the Team Leads with email and complaint in troubleshooting module\\nCheck if AC are working fine\\nCheck if Exhaust is working fine\\n\\n', '2026-01-18 05:00:01', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', NULL, 2, 692, NULL, 1),
