(3685, 2109, 354, '', '', 'At present, the allowed break period for maintaining authorization on the Micro Writer is 45 days. This is not at par with other lithography tools such as the Raith 150 Two.\\nCompared to EBL systems, the Micro Writer is relatively simple in terms of operational complexity. Since its installation, there have been negligible process changes, except for the incorporation of local alignment. In view of this, the current break period appears unnecessarily restrictive.\\nI would therefore request that the allowed break period for the Micro Writer be extended to 90 days.\\nAdditionally, a single fabrication cycle (including measurements) typically takes around 40–50 days to complete. After obtaining results, if a subsequent lithography step is required, the authorization often lapses by that time. This necessitates reappearing for tests or retraining, which leads to avoidable delays in ongoing research work without any clear technical justification.\\nMJB6-100 days\\nDSA-90 days\\nMJB4-100 days\\nRaith 150 Two- 60 days', '2026-01-30 11:49:37', 1, '2026-02-03 12:00:00', NULL, 4, 2527, 2527, 0),
