(3710, 2109, 0, 'Training on tools', '', 'Respected Sir/Madam,\\n\\nThe IITBNF training policy shared via email with the subject “#Important: Update on Training Procedure for IITBNF Tools” states the following:\\n\\n“Training on IITBNF tools will be carried out using IITBNF standard samples and standard recipes. Users are not required to bring their own samples for training. Please plan your training slots accordingly.”\\nIn this regard, I seek clarification on the following points:\\n1. If a user wishes to process their own samples during the training slot, what is the prescribed procedure?\\nKindly let us know whether this needs to be mentioned explicitly while booking the slot, or if it can be communicated through the comments section.\\n2. As per the operators, training is strictly required to be conducted only on IITBNF-provided samples.\\nPlease clarify whether this is a mandatory requirement as per policy, and if so, kindly communicate the same clearly to the operators and users to avoid ambiguity.\\nFrom a user’s perspective, making training on standard samples \\\"mandatory\\\" does not seem optimal it should be \\\"optional\\\". It leads to a significant expenditure of both time and slot charges, without directly contributing to the user’s ongoing research work.\\nMoreover, if there is a concern that training on user-provided samples may compromise process quality or tool safety, this can be adequately addressed by evaluating the user during the test phase and withholding authorization if required.\\nI would appreciate your clarification on the above points so that users can plan their training more effectively and in alignment with the intended policy.\\nMoreover the same policy should be implemented in all the labs including char labs.', '2026-01-30 14:04:48', 2, '2026-02-03 12:00:00', NULL, 4, 2527, 2527, 0),
(3711, 2109, 0, '', '', 'The biometric machine installed in the MCL lab sitting space is not functioning reliably. It works intermittently but fails to operate most of the time, causing inconvenience to users.\\n\\nI kindly request you to look into this issue and arrange for necessary inspection or maintenance at the earliest.', '2026-01-30 14:08:48', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', NULL, 2, 699, 297, 0),
