(3795, 2277, 0, '', '', 'A gas leakage has been detected in the PLD 3 oxygen line. I will carry out my process in the PLD 2 system. \\n\\nThe gas lines for the PLDs are common till inside 1.2 lab, after which they are forked by the blue pipes and the butterfly knobs. So if I open the oxygen line for deposition in PLD 2, can that lead to oxygen leaking from the PLD 3 line somehow?\\n\\nNormally, we keep all the knobs closed, despite which the oxygen was leaking, leading to the emptying of an entire cylinder within days earlier. Oxygen is a serious fire hazard. I\\\'m asking this just to be assured about the safety of using the PLD 2 system. \\n\\nMoreover, once my depositions begin, I will need the system to remain in the same condition for a period of 2 weeks. If there are breaks or changes in between, parameters such as the pressure at the MFC and the laser set energy change significantly, which affects the deposition. Therefore, it would be really helpful if I could be informed when the leakage issue will be resolved.\\n\\nThanks a lot for understanding my concern. ', '2026-02-03 11:54:01', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', NULL, 2, 297, NULL, 0),
(3796, 2336, 354, '', '', 'I have done direct writing with LOR (3B) and PPR (S1813) at 140 doses. After the liftoff, one of the samples didn\\\'t get well, and my feature sizes range between 2 and 10 um. ', '2026-02-03 11:55:19', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', NULL, 1, 89, NULL, 0),
