(3898, 2276, 0, '', '', 'I am writing to respectfully bring to your attention a concern regarding the recently introduced policy stating that users will be trained on IITBNF samples by operators only.\\n\\nWhile we sincerely appreciate the efforts taken to standardize training procedures, we would like to express our concern that training exclusively on IITBNF samples may not fully meet the practical requirements of Ph.D. research work. Different research groups follow distinct protocols and recipes for various tools, which are generally transferred through hands-on training from senior students.\\n\\nAs a result, even after completing training on IITBNF samples, students often need to undergo additional training specific to their respective tools and research methodologies. This leads to an extension of the knowledge transfer timeline and may also result in an unintended waste of time, effort, and resources.\\n\\nWe kindly request you to consider this concern and review the policy accordingly, so that effective and relevant training can be ensured for all research scholars.\\n\\nWe sincerely request that this concern be thoroughly discussed, and after due consideration, we kindly request you to please close this complaint in an appropriate manner.\\n\\nThank you very much for your time and understanding. We look forward to a positive response.', '2026-02-05 14:17:40', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', NULL, 4, 2527, NULL, 0),
