(3941, 2275, 196, '', '', 'Tungsten target got shorted in between deposition.Pls open the chamber and clean it as I need it for deposition  ', '2026-02-06 09:00:34', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', NULL, 1, 89, NULL, 0),
(3942, 1991, 0, 'NA', 'NA', 'I have a concern regarding the recently implemented training policy that applies uniformly to all IITBNF tools.\\n\\nEarlier, training was conducted by group seniors using our own samples. This approach had two key advantages: effective knowledge transfer specific to our research processes, and completion of process training on our actual samples, which saved significant Ph.D. research time and resources.\\n\\nUnder the new policy, training must be conducted on IITBNF samples using baseline recipes, and only operators are allowed to conduct the training. This raises concerns about the efficiency and relevance of the training. For example, in the case of the lithography tool, the resists used by our research group differ from the LOR/PPR baseline resist. Training only on baseline recipes means that after completing the mandatory sessions, additional training with group seniors is still required to learn our actual process. This effectively doubles the training effort and consumes valuable Ph.D. time and resources.\\n\\nCurrently, training for a single tool requires 3–4 hands-on sessions and one authorization test. Each session also has a minimum slot booking duration of 1.5–2 hours, including the authorization test. As a result, a substantial amount of time and money is invested, without directly contributing to our Ph.D research needs.\\n\\nI would like to propose a possible solution to address this. For the four hands-on training sessions, two sessions could be conducted with trained senior students and two with the operator. The authorization test would continue to be conducted by the operator, as was done earlier. Among these sessions, at least one session could be dedicated to baseline recipes, masks, and resists under operator supervision. This hybrid approach would ensure proper safety and tool knowledge, enable effective knowledge transfer from experienced students, and allow students to train on processes relevant to their research.\\n\\nSince slot booking involves significant costs, this approach would help ensure that both time and resources are utilized more effectively, while still maintaining training quality and compliance.\\n\\nI sincerely request that this concern be thoroughly discussed and, after due consideration, please close this request in an appropriate manner.', '2026-02-06 14:59:57', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', NULL, 4, 2527, NULL, 0),
